WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:04.342
It all started one Monday morning at school.

2
00:00:04.402 --> 00:00:08.024
"It" was my idea—my first invention!

3
00:00:08.044 --> 00:00:12.166
We were sitting in class, coloring maps.

4
00:00:12.186 --> 00:00:15.588
I don't understand why our teacher, Mrs.

5
00:00:15.628 --> 00:00:17.669
Romano, makes us color maps.

6
00:00:31.836 --> 00:00:35.437
She acts as if we are in first grade instead of fourth grade.

7
00:00:37.318 --> 00:00:39.998
Does she really think we still like to color?

8
00:00:40.018 --> 00:00:43.219
"Use bright colors!"

9
00:00:43.699 --> 00:00:46.520
Mrs. Romano said, walking around the room.

10
00:00:49.061 --> 00:00:51.042
I colored North America green.

11
00:00:52.282 --> 00:00:54.283
I colored South America orange.

12
00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.924
I colored Africa yellow.

13
00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:04.744
Then I started working on Asia, which is a really big continent.

14
00:01:06.045 --> 00:01:07.646
My hand was getting tired.

15
00:01:08.566 --> 00:01:10.288
I stopped to give it a rest.

16
00:01:12.189 --> 00:01:13.991
My friend Molly leaned toward me.

17
00:01:14.011 --> 00:01:15.452
"Psst, Iggy!"

18
00:01:15.832 --> 00:01:16.533
she whispered.

19
00:01:16.553 --> 00:01:19.675
"My hand hurts from coloring!"

20
00:01:19.695 --> 00:01:21.396
"So does mine!"

21
00:01:21.897 --> 00:01:22.417
I said.

22
00:01:22.437 --> 00:01:24.519
"Quiet, please!"

23
00:01:24.939 --> 00:01:25.459
said Mrs.

24
00:01:25.539 --> 00:01:32.924
Romano. "All I want to hear is the sound of crayons moving across the paper."

25
00:01:34.205 --> 00:01:38.889
Mrs. Romano wanted to hear the sound of crayons moving across the paper?

26
00:01:39.309 --> 00:01:41.311
I was so tired of that sound!

27
00:01:41.331 --> 00:01:45.234
"Why aren't there machines to do coloring?"

28
00:01:45.595 --> 00:01:46.475
I thought suddenly.

29
00:01:46.495 --> 00:01:51.380
"Then kids wouldn't have to work so hard."

30
00:01:53.882 --> 00:01:58.677
That was when I got my idea—a truly incredible idea.

31
00:01:59.997 --> 00:02:03.258
It could make me, Iggy, a famous inventor!

32
00:02:07.379 --> 00:02:10.720
I told Molly about my idea on the way home from school.

33
00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:14.221
"Wow!" said Molly.

34
00:02:14.241 --> 00:02:18.882
"If your idea works, we'll never have to color by hand again!"

35
00:02:20.763 --> 00:02:24.164
Our school is near the apartment building where Molly and I live.

36
00:02:25.224 --> 00:02:27.726
Our apartments are both on the fifth floor.

37
00:02:30.427 --> 00:02:34.250
That means we have to climb a lot of stairs every day.

38
00:02:38.473 --> 00:02:40.834
I wish our backpacks weren't so heavy!"

39
00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:41.855
I groaned.

40
00:02:41.875 --> 00:02:48.339
"Me too," she agreed, panting hard.

41
00:02:56.064 --> 00:02:59.025
I said good-bye to Molly and then went into my apartment.

42
00:03:01.766 --> 00:03:03.706
My mom was on the telephone in the kitchen.

43
00:03:05.787 --> 00:03:07.667
She waved to me as I walked by.

44
00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:13.689
I went into my bedroom and dumped my heavy backpack on the floor.

45
00:03:14.829 --> 00:03:18.470
One of its straps fell just over the chalk line on the floor.

46
00:03:19.431 --> 00:03:24.512
My older brother, Tate, had drawn the line to divide our room into two sections.

47
00:03:25.728 --> 00:03:29.110
"Hey, get your backpack off my side of the room!"

48
00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:30.411
Tate ordered me.

49
00:03:30.431 --> 00:03:33.413
"It's my room too!"

50
00:03:33.433 --> 00:03:34.193
I shot back.

51
00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:37.615
"No arguing, boys!"

52
00:03:38.015 --> 00:03:39.636
called my mother from the kitchen.

53
00:03:40.917 --> 00:03:44.719
I decided to go down to the fourth floor and see my friend Josh.

54
00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.801
I wanted to get away from Tate.

55
00:03:49.402 --> 00:03:52.024
Plus, I needed help with my invention.

56
00:03:54.004 --> 00:03:57.927
I knocked on the door of his apartment, and Josh answered right away.

57
00:03:57.947 --> 00:03:59.308
"Hi, Josh!"

58
00:03:59.669 --> 00:04:00.109
I said.

59
00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:02.591
Josh invited me in.

60
00:04:02.611 --> 00:04:06.114
"Do you know that toy that Sparky likes?"

61
00:04:06.474 --> 00:04:07.255
I blurted out.

62
00:04:09.156 --> 00:04:11.618
Sparky is Josh's pet hamster.

63
00:04:11.638 --> 00:04:14.321
"His seesaw?"

64
00:04:14.641 --> 00:04:15.361
Josh asked.

65
00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:20.385
He walked over to Sparky's cage and lifted up the toy.

66
00:04:20.405 --> 00:04:23.972
"Yes, that's it," I said.

67
00:04:23.992 --> 00:04:25.573
"Can I borrow it?

68
00:04:25.893 --> 00:04:28.113
I want to make one just like it."

69
00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:31.534
"Why?" asked Josh.

70
00:04:32.835 --> 00:04:34.615
"I have a brilliant idea!"

71
00:04:34.975 --> 00:04:35.415
I said.

72
00:04:35.435 --> 00:04:39.517
"I'm going to invent an automatic coloring machine!

73
00:04:39.977 --> 00:04:43.298
My hand will never get tired from coloring again."

74
00:04:45.598 --> 00:04:47.539
Josh's eyes lit up.

75
00:04:47.559 --> 00:04:49.779
"Cool," he said.

76
00:04:49.799 --> 00:04:51.540
"How will it work?"

77
00:04:53.196 --> 00:04:54.177
"You'll see!"

78
00:04:54.477 --> 00:04:55.058
I told him.

79
00:04:55.078 --> 00:04:58.040
"Let's show Sparky's seesaw to Mr.

80
00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:00.502
Calabria, the building superintendent.

81
00:05:00.842 --> 00:05:02.784
He has a lot of wood downstairs."

82
00:05:05.746 --> 00:05:08.308
We went down the steps to the building's basement.

83
00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:15.234
Mr. Calabria was in his workroom surrounded by tools and wood scraps.

84
00:05:17.235 --> 00:05:18.236
He smiled at us.

85
00:05:18.256 --> 00:05:21.699
"Is your kitchen faucet leaking again, Iggy?"

86
00:05:22.019 --> 00:05:22.600
he asked.

87
00:05:23.988 --> 00:05:24.708
I shook my head.

88
00:05:24.728 --> 00:05:27.470
"Our faucet is working fine."

89
00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:30.191
"Then do you have another problem?"

90
00:05:30.551 --> 00:05:31.071
he asked.

91
00:05:31.091 --> 00:05:33.312
"He has something, Mr.

92
00:05:33.352 --> 00:05:35.373
Calabria!" Josh burst out.

93
00:05:35.393 --> 00:05:40.275
"But it's not a problem—it's an amazing, incredible idea!"
